1
00:00:01,244 --> 00:00:03,604
Every video starts as words.

2
00:00:03,604 --> 00:00:05,420
In this studio, the words come

3
00:00:05,994 --> 00:00:09,774
first. The voice you are hearing
was read by an open model,

4
00:00:09,774 --> 00:00:13,140
and the studio knows the moment
each word is spoken.

5
00:00:13,544 --> 00:00:15,914
That timing drives everything.

6
00:00:15,914 --> 00:00:19,404
The captions below are built
from it, two lines at a time,

7
00:00:19,404 --> 00:00:22,344
and each word lights up
as it is said.

8
00:00:22,344 --> 00:00:24,944
Visuals land on their words too.

9
00:00:24,944 --> 00:00:26,600
When I say contrast, a title

10
00:00:27,484 --> 00:00:31,244
appears, and it stays on its
word even if the take changes.

11
00:00:31,244 --> 00:00:34,360
The music steps back
while I speak, and comes forward

12
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:35,844
in the pauses.

13
00:00:35,844 --> 00:00:39,140
Before a render,
the studio checks every frame.

14
00:00:39,444 --> 00:00:41,350
Text sits inside the safe zone,
big

15
00:00:41,984 --> 00:00:45,334
enough to read, with a contrast
of at least four and a half to

16
00:00:45,334 --> 00:00:48,244
one, and it stays long enough
to finish.

17
00:00:48,244 --> 00:00:52,400
After the render, it measures
the file itself. Loudness lands

18
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:55,420
at minus fourteen,
with no flashes and no frozen

19
00:00:56,284 --> 00:00:59,080
frames. Nothing here was checked
by eye alone.

